  "title": "South Etruria Survey area",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/unknown"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The British School at Rome launched the Tiber Valley Project in 1997. Among the goals of this project was an assessment of the regional impact of Rome as an urban center from ca. 1000 B.C. to A.D. 1300 (Patterson et al. 2000). A multi-author monograph reports on the outcomes of the Tiber Valley Project (<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/2533/pleiades/items/PCJZ4UYS/library\" target=\"_self\" title=\"Patterson et al. 20202\">Patterson et al. 2020</a>).</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The original and pioneering South Etruria Survey was led by J.B. Ward-Perkins of the British School at Rome from the 1950s to the 1970s. The initial focus was the territory of the city of Veii (Ager Veientanus). A revisiting of this survey area and the project's outcomes was part of the Tiber Valley Project led by Helen Patterson and initiated in 1997.",
